  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nFirefox has:\n```\nframeset {\n  display: block !important;\n  overflow: clip;\n  position: static !important;\n  float: none !important;\n  border: none !important;\n}\n\nframe {\n  border-radius: 0 !important;\n}\n```\n(and maybe some other custom C++ code?)\n\nChrome & WebKit have:\n```\n    if (m_element && (m_element->hasTagName(frameTag) || m_element->hasTagName(framesetTag))) {\n        // Framesets ignore display, position and float properties.\n        style.setPosition(PositionType::Static);\n        style.setDisplayMaintainingOriginalDisplay(DisplayType::BlockFlow);\n        style.setFloating(Float::None);\n    }\n```\nand:\n```\nframeset {\n    border-color: inherit;\n}\n```\n\nWould be good to standardize and make consistent across browsers.",
